          {
            "creation_time": "2026-10-26T06:07:26Z",
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "bug_id": 19249,
            "text": "Created attachment 3951\nUse direct getClassDef() over redundant isClass()+getClassDef()\n\n`isClass()` is a thin wrapper of `getClassDef()`:\n\n```\nisClass <- function (Class, formal = TRUE, where = topenv(parent.frame())) \n  !is.null(getClassDef(Class, where))\n```\n\nSo, especially in \"hot\" paths, avoiding constructs like\n\n```\nif (isClass(x)) getClassDef(x)\n```\n\nis calling the most expensive piece, `getClassDef()`, twice.\n\nThe attached patch switches to a single `getClassDef()` wherever possible; some \"taste\" might reduce the patch, though I do like the updated code more personally. One consideration is flipping the `if`/`else` branches (`if (is.null(...)) ... else ...`) for possible readability benefit.\n\nThis patch _also_ inherently fixes erroneous usage like `isClass(what, where=packageSlot(ext))` that are tracked separately in Bug #19248.\n\nIn Matrix/R/00_Class.R, which touches this patch >100 times, this patch makes sourcing it ~2-3% faster (end-to-end); timings from 100 times sourcing that file:\n\n```\n# BEFORE\n#    Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max. \n#   1.339   1.362   1.371   1.391   1.397   1.550 \n\n# AFTER\n#    Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max. \n#   1.314   1.335   1.347   1.356   1.375   1.495 \n```\n\nThinner wrappers like `isVirtualClass()` see more speed-up (e.g. 17%), but I think the above end-to-end comparison is indicative that this is a nice low-hanging fruit to squeeze out a few % of performance moreso than a game changer.\n\nWe can also consider an alternative where `isClass()` is changed from being a `getClassDef()` wrapper e.g.\n\n```\nisClass <- function(Class, formal=TRUE, where = topenv(parent.frame())) {                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  if(!is.null(.getClassesFromCache(Class)))  return(TRUE)\n  cname <- classMetaName(if(length(Class) > 1L) Class[[1L]] else Class)\n  package <- if(is.character(where)) where else packageSlot(Class)\n  if(isTRUE(nzchar(package))) {\n    package <- .requirePackage(package)\n    if(is.environment(package) && exists(cname, package)) return(TRUE)\n  }\n  !is.character(where) && exists(cname, where)\n} \n```\n\nBy avoiding `get()`, this can keep some promises lazy, for example.\n\nThat would allow us to keep the `if (exists()) get()` idiom intact with less overhead, but given that `getClassDef()` is already equipped with a `get0()`-like mechanism to give a predictable return value in the `!exists` case, I think the current patch is most appropriate.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/403",
